{%- comment -%}
  Fixed-window rate limit for one scope (spec §12.4). Bounds blast radius per
  identity; not traffic shaping. Uses a per-minute window keyed by
  "<scope>:<window>". The count is incremented with platformOS's atomic
  `increment` (a separate transaction), so concurrent increments within a window
  do not lose updates. A find-then-create race can, under true concurrency, create
  two rows for the same window (documented limitation) — this can only UNDER-count
  slightly at a window boundary, never over-count, so it fails safe for the caller
  and conservative for the limit.

  @param {string}  scope - "principal:<id>" or "client:<id>"
  @param {integer} limit - max requests allowed in the window
  @return {object} { allowed:boolean, count:int, limit:int, retry_after:int } — a blank scope
                   or limit fails closed (allowed: false)
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function object = 'modules/mcp/commands/limits/check/build', scope: scope, limit: limit
  function object = 'modules/mcp/commands/limits/check/check', object: object
  if object.valid
    function out = 'modules/mcp/commands/limits/check/execute', object: object
    return out
  endif

  assign out = {
    "allowed": false,
    "count": 0,
    "limit": limit,
    "retry_after": object.retry_after
  }
  return out
%}
